# 6.9 Device_Limits

## Overview
This section defines architectural limits for device operations, focusing on the absence of restrictions on the number of occurrences for specific events.

## Key Requirement
- **Requirement ID**: DEVLMT-1  
  - **Description**: The device shall not impose any architectural restrictions on the number of times the following events can occur:  
    - Firmware downloads and activation (refer to FWUP-2 for firmware download count);  
    - Changing password during ownership transfer via TCG;  
    - Crypto erase or block erase (format);  
    - Power cycles;  
    - Set/get feature operations (including power state changes);  
    - Log page or debug log retrievals.  
  - This is **not** a test until failure requirement.  

*Note: No numerical limits or test conditions are specified in this requirement.*
